Additonal Feature Discription:
1. Is R a number? - Checks to see if the token to the right of the period
    is a number or not. Numbers on both sides of the period can now be
    represented.
2. Is the first letter of L capitalized? - Checks to see if L is capitalized. This feature
    was chosen because a large number of abbreviations tend to be captilaized. This feature
    captures that fact.
3. The number of times token L appears to the left of a period - Each L across the training dataset
    is counted. This gives the model statistical insight into the data. The main motivation behind
    this feature is to serve as an alternative to using and external list of common abbreviations.

